# Dashboard HTML & CSS conventions

The dashboard opens directly as a file (`file://`) with no build step. Keep it
that way:

- **Inline the data.** Never fetch at runtime — bake values into `data.js` so the
  page works when double-clicked.
- **Use the tokens.** Style with the CSS variables in `styles.css`
  (e.g. `var(--accent)`); don't hardcode hex values in markup.
- **Match the existing cards.** Reuse the `.card` / `.card-head` structure and
  classes already in `dashboard.html` for new sections.
- **Semantic & accessible.** Use real headings (`h2`/`h3`), put `aria-hidden` on
  decorative glyphs, keep contrast readable.
- **Keep files small.** Favor separate files over any single file > 300 lines.

```html
<!-- GOOD: reuse classes, color from a token, data inlined from data.js -->
<article class="card">
  <div class="card-head"><h2>Revenue by GPU type</h2></div>
  <!-- chart bars use var(--accent); no runtime fetch -->
</article>
```
